    "id": "train-7455",
    "question": "Jim decides to open up a bike shop.  The most common repair he does is fixing bike tires.  He charges $20 for this and it cost him $5 in parts.  In one month Jim does 300 of these repairs.  He also does 2 more complex repairs for $300 each and cost $50 in parts.  He also sells $2000 profit worth of things from his retail shop.  If rent and other fixed expense for the shop is $4000 a month how much profit did the shop make?",
    "gold": "3000",
    "answer": "From each tire repair, he made 20-5=$<<20-5=15>>15 profit\nSo repairs made him a profit of 15*300=$<<15*300=4500>>4500\nThe two complex repairs each made him 300-50=$<<300-50=250>>250 profit\nSo those added 250*2=$<<250*2=500>>500\nSo his total profit from everything was 4500+500+2000=$<<4500+500+2000=7000>>7000\nSo he made a profit of 7000-4000=$<<7000-4000=3000>>3000\n#### 3000"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine Jim's profit for the month, we need to calculate his total revenue and total expenses, and then find the difference between them.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the revenue from fixing bike tires:\n- Jim charges $20 for each repair.\n- He does 300 repairs in one month.\n- The cost of parts for each repair is $5.\n\nThe revenue from fixing bike tires is:\n\\[ 20 \\times 300 = 6000 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the revenue from the complex repairs:\n- Jim charges $300 for each repair.\n- He does 2 complex repairs in one month.\n- The cost of parts for each complex repair is $50.\n\nThe revenue from the complex repairs is:\n\\[ 300 \\times 2 = 600 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNow, let's calculate the revenue from selling things from the retail shop:\n- Jim sells $2000 worth of things from his retail shop.\n\nThe revenue from selling things is:\n\\[ 2000 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nAdding all these revenues together gives the total revenue:\n\\[ 6000 + 600 + 2000 = 8600 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the total expenses:\n- The cost of parts for fixing bike tires is $5 per repair.\n- Jim does 300 repairs in one month.\n- The cost of parts for the complex repairs is $50 per repair.\n- Jim does 2 complex repairs in one month.\n- The rent and other fixed expenses for the shop are $4000.\n\nThe total cost of parts for fixing bike tires is:\n\\[ 5 \\times 300 = 1500 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThe total cost of parts for the complex repairs is:\n\\[ 50 \\times 2 = 100 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThe total cost of parts is:\n\\[ 1500 + 100 = 1600 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThe total fixed expenses are:\n\\[ 4000 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nAdding all these expenses together gives the total expenses:\n\\[ 1600 + 4000 = 5600 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nFinally, the profit is the total revenue minus the total expenses:\n\\[ 8600 - 5600 = 3000 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThus, the profit made by the shop in one month is:\n\\[ \\boxed{3000} \\]",
